<title>AUSTRALIA: CRICKET-AUSTRALIA V WEST INDIES FINAL SCOREBOARD.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-AUSTRALIA V WEST INDIES FINAL SCOREBOARD.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Final scoreboard on the fourth</p>
<p>day of the fourth test between Australia and West Indies at</p>
<p>the Adelaide Oval on Tuesday.</p>
<p>West Indies first innings 130 in 47.5 overs (Michael Bevan</p>
<p>four for 31, Shane Warne three for 42)</p>
<p>Australia first innings Australia 517 in 162.3 overs</p>
<p>(Matthew Hayden 125, Greg Blewett 99, Mark Waugh 82, Michael</p>
<p>Bevan 85 not out)</p>
<p>West Indies second innings (overnight 154 for six)</p>
<p> A.Griffith c S.Waugh b McGrath    1</p>
<p> S.Campbell c Taylor b Bevan	24</p>
<p> S.Chanderpaul c Taylor b Bevan    8</p>
<p> B.Lara c Healy b Warne	     78</p>
<p> C.Hooper lbw b Warne		 45</p>
<p> J.Adams c M.Waugh b Bevan	   0</p>
<p> I.Bishop c Bevan b Warne	    0</p>
<p> J.Murray c Taylor b Bevan	  25</p>
<p> C.Walsh c S.Waugh b Bevan	   1</p>
<p> C.Cuffy not out			 3</p>
<p> P.Thompson c Hayden b Bevan	 6</p>
<p> Extras (b-2 lb-5 nb-6)	     13</p>
<p> Total (69.4 overs)		  204</p>
<p>Fall of wickets: 1-6, 2-22, 3-42, 4-138, 5-145, 6-154,</p>
<p>7-181, 8-192, 9-196.</p>
<p>Bowlers: McGrath 17-4-31-1 (nb-5), Bichel 8-4-16-0, Bevan</p>
<p>22.4-3-82-6, Warne 20-4-68-3, Blewett 2-2-0-0.</p>
<p>Result: Australia won by an innings and 183 runs. Australia</p>
<p>won best-of-five match series 3-1. Fifth test begins in Perth on</p>
<p>February 1. </p>
<p>Man of the match: Michael Bevan.</p>
</text>
